Z||000000||Black88GT||07-10-2001||09:26 PM||||Just when ya thought the clutch questions were over.<P><BR>If I am sitting at idle, it chatters, but when I engage it, its quiet.  What causes this?  I looked in my manuals and it said clutch release bearing or input gear bearing.  Which do you guys think?  Any way to test for sure?<P>thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||07-10-2001||10:15 PM||||If it weren't the middle of summer I'd say because it's cold.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But.......it is likely either the input shaft bearing or the throw out bearing (or both).  Did you replace the input shaft  bearing when you replaced the clutch?<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||07-10-2001||10:25 PM||||this is common with some throwout bearings from particular manufacturers. The sound will go away as you put mileage on the car.||||reg||1
